<title>HONG KONG: HK March retail sales up five pct in value on yr.</title>
<headline>HK March retail sales up five pct in value on yr.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-05-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hong Kong's retail sales were a provisional HK$18.6 billion in March, up five percent on the year and up four percent on the month, Census and Statistics Department figures showed.</p>
<p>The following are provisional percentage changes in the value and volume of all retail outlets</p>
<p>						     March    February</p>
<p> Total retail sales (on year)  - value   +5	  -3</p>
<p>					 - volume  +1	  -7</p>
<p>			  (on month) - value   +4	  -20</p>
<p>					 - volume  +3	  -20</p>
<p>Breakdown by category (on year)</p>
<p> Clothing and footwear	   - value   +5	  +4</p>
<p>					 - volume  -6	  -4</p>
<p>Jewellery, watches</p>
<p> clocks, valuable gifts	  - value   -5	  +6</p>
<p>					 - volume  -5	  +10</p>
<p>Consumer durables,</p>
<p> excluding cars		    - value   +6	  +2</p>
<p>					 - volume  +4	  **</p>
<p> Department stores		 - value   +6	  -1</p>
<p>					 - volume  -3	  -7</p>
<p> Supermarkets			- value   +1	  +6</p>
<p>					 - volume  -4	  **</p>
<p> Fuel				  - value   +7	  +9</p>
<p>					 - volume  **	  +1</p>
<p> Motor vehicles		    - value   +30	 +38</p>
<p>					 - volume  +29	 +38</p>
<p>Food, alcoholic drinks and</p>
<p> tobacco			     - value   +1	  +3</p>
<p>					 - volume  +2	  **</p>
<p>** = virtually unchanged</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong newsroom (852) 2843 6441</p>
</text>
